+# Privacy by Design — The Daily Grind website
+
+This document records how the site minimizes, protects and discloses personal
+data, and the results of the third-party audit. Update it whenever a new
+integration, form, cookie or storage key is added.
+
+## 1. Data inventory (this page)
+
+| Data | Where | Purpose | Retention |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `dg:privacy-notice-dismissed` = `"1"` | `localStorage` (browser only) | Don't show the privacy notice again | Until the visitor clears site data |
+| IP address, user agent, URL | In memory for the duration of the HTTP request | Serving the page | **Not logged** by `server.mjs` |
+
+No cookies are set by client-side code. No analytics, advertising, session
+replay, fingerprinting or social widgets are used. The privacy script makes no
+network requests.
+
+Session cookies for `/account`, `/rewards` and `/order-online` belong to the
+backend and are out of scope here. They should be `Secure; HttpOnly;
+SameSite=Lax` (or `Strict`), use the `__Host-` prefix, and contain only an
+opaque session ID.
+
+## 2. Third-party audit — 2026-11-06
+
+| Origin | Was used for | Data exposed | Action |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `images.unsplash.com` | Hero background image | Visitor IP, user agent, Referer (page URL) on every page view | **Removed.** The image is now self-hosted at `assets/img/hero-coffee.jpg` (Unsplash License, photo `1495474472287-4d71bcdd2085`). |
+
+**Current third parties: none.** All resources are same-origin, and the CSP
+(`default-src 'none'`, `'self'` only) enforces that in the browser.
+
+`npm run audit:privacy` (`scripts/privacy-audit.mjs`) re-runs this audit
+automatically and fails if:
+- a non-allowlisted third-party origin is referenced
+- inline scripts, styles or event handlers appear
+- known tracker, analytics or fingerprinting APIs are used
+- client JS writes cookies
+- logout is done through a GET link
+- the `<meta>` CSP drifts from `security-headers.mjs`
+- `_headers` is stale
+
+To add a third party, add it to `THIRD_PARTY_ALLOWLIST` with its purpose, what
+it receives and a review date. Then widen the CSP in `security-headers.mjs` and
+`index.html`, gate loading behind `DailyGrindPrivacy.mayLoadOptional()`, and
+update this file and the public privacy policy.
+
+## 3. Client-side controls (`assets/js/privacy.js`)
+
+- **Global Privacy Control / Do Not Track** are honored. `mayLoadOptional()`
+  returns `false` when either signal is set, and the footer confirms the signal
+  is honored. `/.well-known/gpc.json` declares GPC support.
+- **Tracking parameter stripping:** `utm_*`, `fbclid`, `gclid`, `msclkid` and
+  similar parameters are removed from the address bar with
+  `history.replaceState`. This keeps them out of bookmarks, shared links and
+  onward Referers.
+- **Storage allowlist:** any `dg:`-prefixed storage key that isn't on the
+  allowlist is deleted on load.
+- **Outbound link hardening:** external links get `rel="noopener noreferrer"`
+  and `referrerpolicy="no-referrer"`.
+- **Notice, not a consent wall:** there is nothing optional to consent to, so
+  the notice is informational only.
+
+## 4. Markup
+
+- No inline scripts or styles, so the CSP doesn't need `'unsafe-inline'`.
+- `<meta>` CSP and `<meta name="referrer">` act as fallbacks when the host
+  can't send headers.
+- Logout is a `POST` form. Prefetchers, crawlers and cross-site
+  `<img src="/logout">` can no longer end a session.
+- `robots.txt` keeps account and checkout paths out of search indexes.
+
+## 5. HTTP headers (`security-headers.mjs`)
+
+`server.mjs` (used by `npm start`) sends these headers, and `npm run build`
+writes the same set to `_headers` for Netlify or Cloudflare Pages:
+
+| Header | Value / effect |
+|---|---|
+| Content-Security-Policy | `default-src 'none'`; only same-origin script/style/img/font/connect; `frame-ancestors 'none'`; `form-action 'self'`; `base-uri 'none'` |
+| Strict-Transport-Security | 2 years, includeSubDomains. Add `preload` only after confirming every subdomain serves HTTPS. |
+| Referrer-Policy | `strict-origin-when-cross-origin` (other sites see only the origin) |
+| Permissions-Policy | Denies camera, mic, geolocation, payment, sensors, USB and similar features, plus the Topics, Protected Audience, Attribution Reporting and Shared Storage ad APIs |
+| X-Content-Type-Options | `nosniff` |
+| X-Frame-Options | `DENY` (legacy clickjacking defense) |
+| COOP / CORP / COEP | `same-origin` / `same-origin` / `require-corp` |
+| Cache-Control | HTML: `no-cache, private` (never kept by shared caches); assets: 1 day |
+| X-DNS-Prefetch-Control | `off` |
+
+`server.mjs` also serves only an allowlist of public paths: `index.html`,
+`assets/`, `robots.txt` and `/.well-known/gpc.json`. Source files,
+`package.json` and dotfiles are never exposed. Only `GET`/`HEAD` are accepted,
+and nothing is logged per request.
+
+If the store locator later needs geolocation, change it to
+`geolocation=(self)` on that page only, and request it only after the user
+clicks.
